For sidelink DRX, in case TX UE is configured to use mode1, the SL DRX configuration of RX UE is configured by TX UE’s serving gNB. And according to current 38.331 running CR, the SL DRX configuration of RX UE is included in SL-PHY-MAC-RLC-Config which is determined by DU as shown in following:
SL-PHY-MAC-RLC-Config-v1700 ::=      SEQUENCE {
    sl-DRX-Config-r17                    SetupRelease { SL-DRX-Config-r17 }                                     OPTIONAL,    -- Need M
    ...
}
In Uu interface, CU determines the DRX cycle and passed it to DU. For SL DRX, same rules can be followed.

As specified in TS 38.331, the uplinkTxDirectCurrentTwoCarrierList-r16 is introduced in the RRCReconfigurationComplete message, and the RRCResumeComplete message, to indicate the Tx direct current locations for the configured uplink intra-band CA with two carriers, if requested by the network (see R2-2102207).  
RRCReconfigurationComplete-v1640-IEs ::=    SEQUENCE {
    uplinkTxDirectCurrentTwoCarrierList-r16   UplinkTxDirectCurrentTwoCarrierList-r16                       OPTIONAL,
    nonCriticalExtension              RRCReconfigurationComplete-v1700-IEs                                    OPTIONAL
}

In the CU/DU split architecture, when the gNB-CU receives the uplinkTxDirectCurrentTwoCarrierList-r16 from the UE, it should deliver it to the gNB-DU for L1 configuration in the UE context modification request message. Note that for Rel-15, the Uplink TxDirectCurrentList Information is already indicated.

